{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And she said: If you give a pledge.</b> Some explain that he had relations with her by way of kiddushin, and thus they interpret: מה תתן לי כי תבוא אלי — meaning, with what will you betroth me? And he said: אנכי אשלח גדי עזים etc. And she said: אם תתן ערבון etc. And he said etc. And she said: חותמך ופתילך etc. — meaning, your signet ring with which you seal, and he betrothed her with the ring. And the question of R. Moshe: what did the kiddushin accomplish, for witnesses are required, and even if both of them agree, as is stated in tractate Kiddushin. And one may answer that presumably an important person such as Judah would not go out on the road without two others with him, like a Torah scholar, and he betrothed her in their presence. And if you ask: still, how did the kiddushin help, for he did not give her the ring except as a pledge, and we say in Kiddushin: if he betrothed her with a perutah and left a pledge with her, she is not betrothed. And one may answer that he transferred the ring to her at that time completely; only afterward he stipulated with her that if he sends a kid of the goats she would return the ring to him, as above."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:39.316905172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}